```

===== STAGE 4 : EXPLANATION & PROOF =====
The problem asks for the smallest integer greater than 200 for which \( \text{gcd}(n, 36) = 18 \). We derived that \( n \) must be of the form \( n = 18k \) with \( k \) being odd. The smallest \( k \) such that \( 18k > 200 \) is \( k = 12 \) (since \( 18 \times 12 = 216 \)). 

