The problem asks for the total area of the shaded regions in rectangle \(ABCD\) after subtracting the areas of the equilateral triangles. The area of the rectangle is calculated as \(24\sqrt{3}\) and the total area of the three equilateral triangles is \(3\sqrt{3}\). Thus, the shaded area is given by:

\[
\text{Shaded Area} = \text{Area of Rectangle} - \text{Total Area of Triangles} = 24\sqrt{3} - 3\sqrt{3} = 21\sqrt{3}
\]

The code in Stage 2 correctly implements this calculation, confirming that the shaded area is \(21\sqrt{3}\). The output from Stage 3 matches this calculation.

