===== STAGE 2 : PYTHON CODE =====
```python
def solve():
    angle_A = 39
    angle_QBP = 14
    
    # Let angle_B = b and angle_C = c
    # We know that b + c = 141
    # Also, angle_ABP = b / 3 and angle_ACQ = c / 3
    # Therefore, angle_BPC = 180 - angle_ABP - angle_ACQ
    # angle_BPC = 180 - (b / 3) - (c / 3)
    
    # From b + c = 141, we can express c as 141 - b
    # angle_BPC = 180 - (b / 3) - ((141 - b) / 3)
    # angle_BPC = 180 - (b + 141 - b) / 3
    # angle_BPC = 180 - 141 / 3
    # angle_BPC = 180 - 47
    angle_BPC = 133
    
    return angle_BPC
```

