  \]
  \[
  \text{min\_y} = \max(0, 2 - (k - 1)), \quad \text{max\_y} = \min(5 - k, 2)
  \]

The code correctly counts the valid positions for each square size and sums them up. The final output of \(25\) confirms that there are \(25\) squares containing the center square.

