\[
\text{Outer Area} = 100 + 2l + 2w + 4
\]

The area of the outer dark gray strip is:

\[
\text{Outer Dark Gray Area} = \text{Outer Area} - \text{Inner Area} = (100 + 2l + 2w + 4) - 100 = 2l + 2w + 4
\]

For \( l = 10 \) and \( w = 10 \), we find \( 2(10) + 2(10) + 4 = 44 \). The output from Stage 3 confirms this calculation.

