2. The hour hand moves at 30 degrees per hour plus 0.5 degrees per minute: \( \text{Hour Angle} = 30 \times \text{hours} + 0.5 \times \text{minutes} \).
At 2:48, the hour is 2 and the minutes are 48. We calculate both angles and find the absolute difference. The smaller angle is the minimum of this difference and \(360 - \text{difference}\).

===== STAGE 2 : PYTHON CODE =====
