The code calculates the modular inverse of \( 12{,}500{,}000 \) modulo \( 999{,}999{,}999 \) and then computes \( n \) as \( (111 \cdot \text{inv\_a}) \mod 999{,}999{,}999 \). The expected return value of `solve()` is computed to be \( 111 \).

