\]
We are provided that \(\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{a}} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 13 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}\). This implies that \(\mathbf{a}\) can be expressed in terms of its components. Since \(\mathbf{a}\) and \(\mathbf{b}\) are orthogonal, we can find \(\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 13 \end{pmatrix}\) using the relationship between projections onto orthogonal vectors.

===== STAGE 2 : PYTHON CODE =====
